1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,760
足迹交易课程。第14单元。
The Footprint Course. Unit 14.

2
00:00:03,240 --> 00:00:04,980
Delta 头寸解除。
The Delta Position Unwind.

3
00:00:05,320 --> 00:00:08,940
这是30天挑战的第26天。
This is Challenge Day 26 of 30. In the following slide,

4
00:00:09,080 --> 00:00:13,599
在下一张幻灯片中，我们将聚焦几条关键规则，来理解金融市场，包括核心玩家，他们的目标，
we are going to focus on some of the key rules

5
00:00:13,599 --> 00:00:17,707
to understand about the financial markets, including the key participants,

6
00:00:17,707 --> 00:00:23,458
the objectives of these participants, the skills required to be successful as a trader,

7
00:00:23,458 --> 00:00:27,977
and some of the skills and processes that various traders have.

10
00:00:53,760 --> 00:00:57,480
首先，最关键的是：谁是你的对手？
The first and most important thing to understand is, who are you playing against?

12
00:00:57,560 --> 00:01:00,741
交易这场博弈中的玩家都有谁？
Who are the players in this game or in this game of trading?

13
00:01:00,741 --> 00:01:04,400
市场中有多种玩家，我将它们总结为5类。
Now, there is a number of different players, and I’ve summarized them into five.

15
00:01:04,540 --> 00:01:09,468
第一类也是最大的玩家：养老金、对冲基金、机构、银行。我们称它们为影响型玩家。
So, the first—and the biggest—players being your pension funds, your hedge funds,

16
00:01:09,468 --> 00:01:13,340
your institutions, your banks. These are what we call influential players.

18
00:01:13,420 --> 00:01:17,940
换句话说，它们的决策能操控价格走势。
In other words, they can move prices around based on the decisions that they make.

20
00:01:18,260 --> 00:01:24,960
但现实是，我们谁都无法影响市场，
Okay. Now, no one—none of us, not myself included—none of us are influential in the market

22
00:01:24,960 --> 00:01:28,503
无法像它们那样操控价格，让价格随心所欲涨跌。
to the extent that we can actually manipulate or, rather, maneuver prices

23
00:01:28,503 --> 00:01:31,751
and actually make prices go up and down. So, straight away,

24
00:01:31,752 --> 00:01:36,163
所以，你要先问自己，‘我不是影响型玩家。’ 下一类是投机型玩家。
you’ve got to say to yourself, 'Well, I’m not an influential player.'

25
00:01:36,163 --> 00:01:38,999
The next type of player is a speculative player.

27
00:01:39,080 --> 00:01:46,407
这里的投机型玩家，更偏向于有影响力的类型。
Now, again, a speculative player in this definition, we try to include or more lean toward gain-influential type players.

29
00:01:46,407 --> 00:01:48,927
比如对冲基金，对某个市场有方向性判断，要么被止损出局，要么不被。
In other words, we’re looking at hedge funds

30
00:01:48,927 --> 00:01:52,288
that are taking a directional view on whatever market it may be,

31
00:01:52,288 --> 00:01:55,088
and they either get stopped out, or they don’t.

33
00:01:55,090 --> 00:01:59,180
它们不会持有产品或资产类别，直到到期或类似节点。
They’re not holding that product or that asset class until maturity or something like that.

36
00:01:59,180 --> 00:02:04,400
所以下一类玩家是投机型玩家。
So, the next type of player is a speculative player.

37
00:02:04,560 --> 00:02:11,047
但这不包括我们这些散户、日内交易者或短线交易者。
Again, that does not include us as a retail market, as day traders, as short-term traders.

38
00:02:11,047 --> 00:02:13,479
然后是高频交易者。
We then have the high-frequency traders.

40
00:02:13,580 --> 00:02:17,340
这可能包括部分开发了算法的你。
Now, again, this might include some of you, some of you that have developed algorithms.

42
00:02:17,340 --> 00:02:19,740
这也包括你。 关键在于理解
This includes you. The important thing to understand

43
00:02:19,740 --> 00:02:24,398
关于高频交易者的策略特点,其一，策略极其精确,其二，风险与收益都非常明确。
with regards to the players that play in high frequency,

44
00:02:24,398 --> 00:02:28,125
they develop strategies that, one, are very exact,

45
00:02:28,125 --> 00:02:32,318
and, two, have very specific both risk and reward.

48
00:02:32,320 --> 00:02:36,260
稍后在策略开发部分会详细展开。
And we’ll talk a little bit about that later when we go into actual strategy development.

49
00:02:36,380 --> 00:02:38,772
包括我、自营交易者、专业交易者,以及你们中的很多人。 你们属于日内交易者。
That’s myself, your prop traders, your professional traders,

50
00:02:38,772 --> 00:02:40,366
as well as many of you.

51
00:02:42,900 --> 00:02:45,540
当然，还有波段交易者。
And then, obviously, swing traders.

52
00:02:45,540 --> 00:02:48,200
日内与波段交易者的区别仅在于持仓时间。
between a day trader and a swing trader is merely the time frame over which we’re holding.

54
00:02:48,200 --> 00:02:51,060
日内交易者更短线，波段交易者更中长线。
Day traders are a little bit more short-term; swing traders are a little bit more long-term.

55
00:02:51,260 --> 00:02:54,201
了解这些玩家很重要，因为知道自己是谁，对手是谁,你就能立刻给自己定位。
Now, it’s important to understand these players

56
00:02:54,201 --> 00:02:59,348
because if you know which player you are and who you’re up against,

57
00:02:59,348 --> 00:03:04,863
straight away, you’re almost going to put yourself in a division of the players.

58
00:03:04,865 --> 00:03:09,278
你会说，‘我属于这类玩家。’
You’re going to say, *‘Well, I’m one of these players,’*

61
00:03:09,340 --> 00:03:11,513
不仅是目标，还有技能和流程,这才是你需要走的方向。
Not just objective, the skills and the process,

62
00:03:11,513 --> 00:03:15,589
but this is ultimately the direction or the path that I need to go down.

63
00:03:15,590 --> 00:03:19,343
如果你是日内或波段交易者,我现在先给你概括三点：
Now, if you are a day trader or a swing trader,

64
00:03:19,343 --> 00:03:23,438
I'm going to outline for you now, first, what is your objective?

65
00:03:23,438 --> 00:03:23,779
Secondly,

66
00:03:24,020 --> 00:03:26,700
第二，你需要哪些技能？ 第三，流程是什么？
what are the skills you need? And then third, what is the process?

67
00:03:27,080 --> 00:03:28,880
这正是今晚课程的核心。
And that’s where the core of tonight’s entire session is going to be.

69
00:03:28,880 --> 00:03:36,500
作为日内/波段交易者，首要目标是培养稳定性。
So, your objective as a day trader/swing trader, first and foremost, is to develop consistency.

70
00:03:36,500 --> 00:03:40,350
复盘策略时，你要问自己,做每日总结、头脑风暴新想法时，要问：第一，‘我是日内还是波段交易者？’
Now, what you need to ask yourself when you review your strategies,

71
00:03:40,350 --> 00:03:44,200
when you do your daily debriefs, when you’re brainstorming new ideas,

72
00:03:44,200 --> 00:03:50,297
is this: firstly, ‘I am a day trader or a swing trader.’ Secondly, ‘What I’m doing right now—

75
00:03:50,380 --> 00:04:00,860
‘我现在做的这件事，能推动我实现稳定性目标吗？’
this hour I’m spending on whatever task—is this ultimately moving me toward that objective of consistency?’ Okay.

78
00:04:00,860 --> 00:04:03,192
有时有人发给我一张高时间框架的日线图,问，‘持仓3周获利10%，你怎么看？’
sometimes someone sends me a long higher-timeframe daily chart

79
00:04:03,192 --> 00:04:05,524
and asks, ‘What do you think about holding this

80
00:04:05,524 --> 00:04:07,597
for the next three weeks for a 10% gain?’

81
00:04:07,640 --> 00:04:10,800
我会说，‘先等等。’
I’ll say, ‘Hold on a second.’

83
00:04:10,920 --> 00:04:14,540
你是机构型玩家？还是投机型玩家？
Are you an institutional player? Are you a speculative player?

84
00:04:14,540 --> 00:04:24,220
你能舒服地持有大额头寸数天吗？ 对99%的人，答案是不能。
Can you comfortably hold a large capital position for multiple days?’ For 99% of us, the answer is no. Okay.

87
00:04:24,240 --> 00:04:29,102
要培养稳定性，你需更频繁地交易
So, to develop consistency, you’ll need to trade more frequently.

88
00:04:29,102 --> 00:04:36,140
而要频繁交易，你不能只做一两笔或每月几笔交易
And to trade more frequently, you cannot be taking One or two or three or monthly-type trades.

92
00:04:36,180 --> 00:04:39,460
所以，我们要根据玩家来定目标
So, you see how we outline the players to the objective.

93
00:04:39,700 --> 00:04:45,700
不同玩家的风险管理差异极大
Then, the risk management of all of these different players varies very differently.

95
00:04:45,700 --> 00:04:51,120
影响型玩家或投机型玩家，
So, an influential player or a speculative player, they can sit with massively wide stops.

96
00:04:51,120 --> 00:04:53,660
止损可能设在4%、5%或10%
We’re talking four, five, 10% stops.

97
00:04:54,100 --> 00:04:56,060
他们会对冲大部分策略
They’ll hedge most of those strategies.

98
00:04:56,220 --> 00:04:59,341
他们的风险管理方式与我们日内或波段交易者完全不同甚至与高频交易者也不同
They have a very, very different risk management approach

99
00:04:59,341 --> 00:05:02,809
to what we do as day traders and swing traders,

100
00:05:02,809 --> 00:05:04,196
and even high-frequency traders.

101
00:05:04,440 --> 00:05:07,416
五类玩家中，高频交易者的风险管理系统最独特他们总是承受很小的损失
Of all five of the players, high-frequency traders

102
00:05:07,416 --> 00:05:10,020
have the most unique risk management system,

103
00:05:10,020 --> 00:05:13,740
in that they take very small losers all the time.

104
00:05:13,740 --> 00:05:18,300
但赚钱时能赚回更多
But when they make money, they’re actually making a lot more than what they’re losing.

106
00:05:18,460 --> 00:05:24,980
接下来，目标是每天盈利
Then, our next objective is to print green every single day. Now, that objective differs.

108
00:05:25,340 --> 00:05:28,473
如果是波段交易者，周一到周三的回撤可能可以接受只要周四周五能扭亏为盈
If you’re a swing trader, it might be okay

109
00:05:28,473 --> 00:05:31,293
to have a few drawdowns for Monday, Tuesday, Wednesday,

110
00:05:31,293 --> 00:05:35,366
so long as Thursday, Friday, when you do go long or make money,

111
00:05:35,366 --> 00:05:37,559
it makes back all of those losses.

113
00:05:37,680 --> 00:05:40,640
最后一个目标是杠杆
And then, the last objective is leverage.

114
00:05:41,220 --> 00:05:44,480
影响型玩家的杠杆使用远低于我们这些日内和波段交易者
Influential players don’t tend to use as much leverage as we do as day traders and swing traders.

115
00:05:44,480 --> 00:05:47,160
高频交易者的杠杆目标
High-frequency traders have a very different objective

116
00:05:47,160 --> 00:05:50,222
与我们的目标不同
when it comes to leverage than we do

117
00:05:52,520 --> 00:06:01,360
所以，首先得明确：你是哪类玩家？
So, it’s important to understand, number one, what player are you? Based on that player, what is your objective?

119
00:06:01,980 --> 00:06:05,350
明确目标后，
Once you know what your objective is,

120
00:06:05,350 --> 00:06:08,720
就能轻松确定
then it’s very simple to determine:

121
00:06:08,720 --> 00:06:14,498
你需要掌握哪些技能
What are the skills that you are going to need to learn

123
00:06:15,960 --> 00:06:22,640
第一是一致性。这种一致性技能，你若频繁更换策略是无法培养的
The first is consistency. This consistency skill, you're not going to develop by chopping and changing your strategies,

125
00:06:22,640 --> 00:06:31,203
频繁更换策略无法培养稳定性今天交易期货，明天交易权益
by looking at various different markets, trading futures one day, then trading equities, by following some guy on Twitter

127
00:06:31,203 --> 00:06:34,358
然后执行他抛出的所有交易
and taking whatever trades he spins out.

129
00:06:34,360 --> 00:06:39,080
接下来是纪律
The next is discipline.

130
00:06:44,740 --> 00:06:47,503
一致性。第二是纪律
Consistency. The second is discipline.

131
00:06:47,503 --> 00:06:53,583
说到纪律，你如何培养纪律？
With regard to discipline, how are you going to develop discipline?

132
00:06:53,583 --> 00:06:55,245
培养纪律的唯一方法是经历不同的市场情境不同时间段、一天中的不同时间一周中的不同日子。这是唯一学习方式
The only way to develop discipline

133
00:06:55,245 --> 00:06:57,739
is to be in a number of different situations

134
00:06:57,739 --> 00:07:01,619
over different periods of time, different times of day, different days of the week.

135
00:07:01,619 --> 00:07:03,836
That's the only way you're going to learn

136
00:07:04,768 --> 00:07:08,480
如果你每天只做一笔交易能培养出日内或波段交易的纪律吗？可能不行
If you're sitting in trades and only doing one trade a day,

137
00:07:08,480 --> 00:07:12,501
are you going to develop discipline as a day trader or swing trader?

138
00:07:13,340 --> 00:07:17,240
你需要培养的下一个技能是耐心
The next skill you need to develop is patience.

139
00:07:18,160 --> 00:07:19,806
如何培养耐心？
How are you going to develop patience?

140
00:07:19,806 --> 00:07:21,216
你不会通过下单后设置止损和止盈就不管了来培养耐心
You're not going to develop patience

141
00:07:21,216 --> 00:07:24,977
by putting in a trade in the market, then putting in a stop and a target,

142
00:07:25,920 --> 00:07:30,380
观察市场能让你学到很多信息
By watching it, you're going to learn and take away a lot of information from the market.

144
00:07:30,380 --> 00:07:34,765
你需要培养的最后一个技能是我所谓的传统痛阈真正的决心和韧性。培养这些的唯一方法
The last skill you're going to need to develop

145
00:07:34,765 --> 00:07:39,637
is what I like to call good old-fashioned pain threshold,

146
00:07:39,637 --> 00:07:41,586
real determination and grit.

147
00:07:46,460 --> 00:07:55,718
唯一度过困难期的方式就是大量交易
the only way you're going to get through the hard knocks is by ultimately doing a lot of trading.

151
00:07:55,940 --> 00:08:03,760
通过这些交易磨练自己
Going through those trades, really just trying to develop yourself through the hard knocks.

153
00:08:04,820 --> 00:08:07,361
所以一旦我们理解了市场玩家然后根据我们的角色和所需技能确定目标为了实现目标，我们进入流程环节
so once we have developed an understanding of the players in the market,

154
00:08:07,361 --> 00:08:09,902
then we determine what our objective is based on the player we are,

155
00:08:09,902 --> 00:08:12,443
as well as the skills we need in order to achieve that objective,

156
00:08:12,443 --> 00:08:13,616
we then move to the process.

158
00:08:13,980 --> 00:08:16,003
流程很简单，我希望你记下来这周好好思考：你作为交易者的优势和劣势是什么？
Okay, now the process is very simple,

159
00:08:16,003 --> 00:08:19,472
and I want you to write this down and think about it

160
00:08:19,472 --> 00:08:21,206
over the course of the week.

161
00:08:21,206 --> 00:08:24,097
Firstly, what are your strengths and weaknesses as a trader?

162
00:08:25,158 --> 00:08:28,323
you should be able to outline, I’m really good at trading volatile markets.

163
00:08:28,323 --> 00:08:30,358
I really like it when the markets are fast,

164
00:08:32,360 --> 00:08:37,680
有突破、干净的突破，市场激烈波动。我喜欢这种状态
there are breakouts, there are a lot of clean breaks, the market’s moving aggressively. I really like that.

166
00:08:37,740 --> 00:08:39,280
把它写下来，作为你的优势
And you write it down as a strength.

167
00:08:39,560 --> 00:08:43,300
同样，写下你作为交易者的弱点
You then do the same and write down what your weaknesses are as a trader.

169
00:08:43,560 --> 00:08:45,852
好，如果你风险管理很差或无法坚持交易直到目标达成，就记下来
Okay, if you’re very bad at risk management,

170
00:08:45,852 --> 00:08:49,163
or you’re really bad at being disciplined, at sticking through the trade

171
00:08:49,163 --> 00:08:52,219
until it’s achieved what it should, then you write that down.

173
00:08:52,220 --> 00:08:53,920
好，原因很简单你要基于优势而非弱点来制定策略
Okay, again, the reason is,

174
00:08:53,920 --> 00:08:59,360
you will start to develop a strategy based on your strengths and not your weaknesses, right?

176
00:08:59,540 --> 00:09:04,715
如果你不擅长突破交易，就别做突破交易者
There is zero point in trying to be a breakout trader if you’re bad at breakouts, right?

177
00:09:04,715 --> 00:09:06,440
这完全没有意义
There’s just no point, right?

179
00:09:06,540 --> 00:09:10,340
在模式识别部分，我会展示这些如何整合
Now, when I get to the pattern recognition part, I’m going to show you how this all molds together.

181
00:09:11,100 --> 00:09:15,780
或者说，你在整个市场中处于什么位置？
Then, where do you fit in? In other words, where do you fit in into this whole market?

184
00:09:16,020 --> 00:09:18,160
你是剥头皮交易者吗？
Are you a trader that scalps?

185
00:09:18,220 --> 00:09:20,900
还是喜欢持仓几小时？
Are you a trader that likes to sit for a couple of hours on a trade?

187
00:09:20,900 --> 00:09:23,120
你偏好什么类型的交易？
What kind of trades do you like to do?

188
00:09:23,440 --> 00:09:25,880
你在哪种情况下最舒服？
Where do you feel most comfortable?

189
00:09:25,940 --> 00:09:28,980
你喜欢市场主动来找你，被动入场？
Do you prefer the market coming to you, and you’re getting in passively?

191
00:09:29,100 --> 00:09:32,580
还是主动提供流动性？
Or do you prefer to be aggressive and provide liquidity to the market?

193
00:09:39,780 --> 00:09:42,961
希望那次导师课让你真正理解以及为什么要知晓这点如此重要以及谁最终创造了哪种策略
Hopefully, that mentor session really drove home the understanding

194
00:09:42,961 --> 00:09:46,495
behind the different participants and why it’s so important

195
00:09:46,495 --> 00:09:50,383
to know who you’re actually interacting with in the market,

196
00:09:50,383 --> 00:09:52,857
and who’s ultimately creating which strategy.

198
00:09:52,860 --> 00:09:56,808
这显然是我们模板的重要部分也是判断交易策略成功概率高低的重要原则
It is obviously a very important part of our template,

199
00:09:56,808 --> 00:10:00,361
as it is a very important principle for identifying

200
00:10:00,361 --> 00:10:04,704
when a trade strategy will have a higher probability of success

201
00:10:04,704 --> 00:10:06,678
or lower probability of success.

203
00:10:07,080 --> 00:10:10,980
下一个策略，仍是逆势交易策略
Now, in the next strategy, this is obviously a counter-trading strategy again.

205
00:10:12,260 --> 00:10:19,480
是我们上下文与足迹策略的第三个
In terms of, it’s no longer standalone, this is the third of our context and footprint strategies.

207
00:10:20,020 --> 00:10:23,720
它需要非常激进的执行方法
And obviously, it requires a very aggressive execution methodology.

208
00:10:27,890 --> 00:10:30,790
这是适合耐心交易者的策略
This is a little bit of a patient trader’s strategy.

209
00:10:31,030 --> 00:10:32,370
需要极大的耐心
This does require a lot of patience.

210
00:10:33,570 --> 00:10:38,190
这种策略不会总是出现
It’s one of those strategies that you won't necessarily always see.

212
00:10:38,370 --> 00:10:40,010
多数情况下，可能在盘尾才会看到
A lot of the time, you'll see it maybe at the end of the day.

213
